.TH SWAYDESK-CLICK-CATCHER 1 2026-11-16 "swaydesk 0.1.6" "Sway desktop components"
.SH NAME
swaydesk\-click\-catcher \- close the launcher with a click outside it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaydesk\-click\-catcher
.B \-\-pid
.I PID
.SH DESCRIPTION
While the process
.I PID
runs, covers every monitor with an almost transparent layer, under the launcher and above the windows. A click on it ends the process (SIGTERM), as Esc closes the launcher, and the end of the process ends this one.
.PP
sway\-launcher starts it next to rofi (Alt+Space and the window search). rofi 1.7 runs through Xwayland and never sees a click on a Wayland window, and rofi 2.0 only sees clicks on its menu; rofi 2.1 handles the click outside by itself, and its own layer then covers this one.
.PP
The process is followed through a pidfd, so a reused process number never gets the signal. It takes no keyboard input.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-pid " PID"
The process to close on a click, and to wait for.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the process ends (or had already ended), 1 if the display can't be opened, 2 on a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rofi (1),
.BR swaydesk (7)
